# ==============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — Aegis Forge
# ==============================================================================
# Every path below requires review from its listed owner(s) before merge.
# Combined with branch protection (see SETUP.md §Branch Protection), this
# enforces Segregation of Duties on security-sensitive surfaces.
#
# The baseline repo is owned by a single maintainer, so all entries point to
# @mochrzlf. @pakel123 is added as a co-owner on the default rule so that a
# second account can satisfy the "code owner review" branch-protection rule
# (GitHub forbids the PR author from approving their own PR, and @mochrzlf
# authors every PR). In a derived project with a real team, replace these with
# your actual users/teams (e.g. @your-org/security-lead) to restore the
# intended Segregation of Duties. Syntax:  <pattern>  <owner> [<owner>...]
# ==============================================================================

# Default owner for anything not matched below
*                                           @mochrzlf @pakel123

